Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.16.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.16.0 attacks the remaining occasional content flash reported with archive 16. The 0.15.0 visual kit works: the log shows 15 layer-drop episodes in the Safari session but the user saw only one flash, so the snapshot pad and the transparent not-hosting background are masking the black windows. The remaining visible flash comes from two new sources pinned by the archive. First, every updateSettingsWithBlock call costs one full scene resubmission (contentState 2-0-1-2), and the preventive tier was writing 2 to 4 times per deactivation episode (the first write fast, then repeats every 250 ms) without actually stopping the drops; the drops that did happen were recovered by the level-1 write and masked by the pad anyway. Second, right after a real-black recovery the presenter reasserts its own geometry on the presentation view (the archive shows 384x562 versus the 362x366 target, a 54 percent deviation), and the 500 ms correction throttle let the wrong size stay visible for up to 700 ms before snapping back. 0.16.0 therefore adds a preventive write cooldown (new key keepAlivePreventCooldownMs = 2000): the first write of an episode still fires fast at 250 ms, but any further write in the same episode waits 2 seconds; zero disables the cooldown for A/B work. It also opens a 2-second geometry-hold window after every real-black recovery: during that window the presentation view frame is checked and corrected every single tick, compressing the wrong-size window to at most one tick (200 ms). The correction log line is tagged with the hold state. Config version migrates 16 to 17.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
